    m_recon_elbow, ": beyond this point, additional components reduce reconstruction\n",
    "     RMSE by less than", recon_selection_threshold_pct, "% each — diminishing returns.\n")
cat("  3) Preliminary out-of-sample AR(1) forecast RMSE is minimized at m =", m_forecast_best,
    "; m =", m_forecast_parsimonious, "is the smallest m within", forecast_tolerance_pct,
    "% of that minimum forecast RMSE.\n")
cat("  4) m =", recommended_m, "= max(", m_recon_elbow, ",", m_forecast_parsimonious,
    ") is the SMALLEST FPC dimension that satisfies BOTH the reconstruction-adequacy\n",
    "     criterion AND the forecast-adequacy criterion simultaneously.\n")
cat("  5) At m =", recommended_m, ": reconstruction RMSE =",
    round(fpc_selection_table$reconstruction_rmse[fpc_selection_table$m == recommended_m], 5),
    ", forecast RMSE =", round(fpc_selection_table$forecast_rmse[fpc_selection_table$m == recommended_m], 5), "\n")
if (recommended_m < m_95) {
  cat("  NOTE: the recommended m is SMALLER than the m needed to reach even 95%\n",
      "  cumulative variance (m =", m_95, "). This is expected and intentional: it\n",
      "  demonstrates concretely why variance-explained alone would have recommended\n",
      "  a larger, less parsimonious model than the reconstruction/forecast evidence\n",
      "  actually supports.\n", sep = "")
} else if (recommended_m > m_99) {
  cat("  NOTE: the recommended m is LARGER than the m needed to reach 99% cumulative\n",
