cat("\n================= MAIN METHODOLOGICAL QUESTION =================\n")
cat(
  "Does modelling the", p, "FPC scores JOINTLY (Step 10-11's FSSM, coupled only\n",
  "through shared H/Q covariance structure) forecast BETTER than modelling each\n",
  "score INDEPENDENTLY (this step, each score its own auto.arima/ETS)?\n\n",
  "Aggregate result: joint FSSM wins on", n_joint_wins, "of", n_total_metrics, "summary metrics;\n",
  "per-component result: joint FSSM wins on", sum(per_component_comparison$joint_better),
  "of", p, "individual FPCs.\n\n",
  if (n_joint_wins >= ceiling(n_total_metrics / 2)) {
    paste0("On balance, the evidence FAVOURS the joint FSSM here. Since the FSSM's\n",
           "ONLY structural advantage over independent forecasting is shared H/Q\n",
           "covariance estimation (Step 11's chosen structure couples the components'\n",
           "NOISE, never their dynamics directly -- recall Z_t/T remain purely diagonal\n",
           "even in the 'full' H/Q variants), this result would suggest that pooling\n",
           "information about the SCALE/CO-VARIATION of estimation noise across\n",
           "components genuinely helps -- plausibly because with p=19 components and\n",
           "n_train~1748 days, some individual components are too short/noisy to\n",
           "support a fully independent, richly-parameterized univariate model, and\n",
           "borrowing strength through a shared covariance structure regularizes them.\n")
  } else {
    paste0("On balance, the evidence does NOT clearly favour the joint FSSM here --\n",
           "independent per-component forecasting matches or beats it on a majority of\n",
           "metrics. This is a genuinely informative negative result: it suggests the\n",
           "FSSM's added structural complexity (a custom time-varying Hadamard loading\n",
           "matrix, joint ML estimation across 19 dimensions) is not earning its keep\n",
           "over simply letting each FPC's own conventional ARIMA/ETS order be chosen\n",
           "on its own merits. Since Step 11's H/Q variants never introduce genuine\n",
           "CROSS-COMPONENT dynamics (Z_t/T stay diagonal throughout), this is broadly\n",
           "consistent with there being little exploitable cross-score dependence for\n",
           "the FSSM's shared-covariance structure to capture in the first place.\n")
  },
  "\nEITHER WAY, this comparison isolates the SCORE-FORECASTING METHOD as the sole\n",
  "variable (the daily-level forecast is IDENTICAL in both pipelines, reused\n",
  "from Step 14), so the result above is attributable specifically to joint vs.\n",
  "independent score dynamics -- not confounded by any other modelling choice.\n",
  "A formal statistical test of whether this difference is significant (e.g.\n",
  "Diebold-Mariano on the paired forecast errors) is explicitly left to Step 19,\n",
  "consistent with this project's roadmap.\n",
  sep = "")
cat("===================================================================\n")

