## =============================================================================
## STEP 18 — ROLLING-ORIGIN FORECAST VALIDATION OF ALL GROUNDWATER FORECASTING
##           MODELS
## Project : Hourly Groundwater Level (GWL) analysis — well GT2648C03
## Continues directly from STEPS 5, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17.
## =============================================================================
## PURPOSE OF STEP 18
## Every prior benchmarking step (15-17) evaluated only ONE-STEP-AHEAD
## accuracy. This step extends that to a genuine ROLLING-ORIGIN, MULTI-HORIZON
## design (h = 1..7 days), for all five model families, using IDENTICAL
## origins and target dates across models and horizons so every comparison
## is apples-to-apples. It is the primary evidentiary step for the project.
##
## FIVE MODEL FAMILIES COMPARED (per the roadmap):
##   1. Persistence            (Step 15's definition, generalized to horizon h:
##                              GWL_hat_{d+h}(hour) = GWL_d(hour), i.e. the
##                              origin day's own actual curve, repeated)
##   2. ARIMA (Step 16)         daily LEVEL only -- functional ISE not applicable
##   3. ETS (Step 16)           daily LEVEL only -- functional ISE not applicable
##   4. FPCA + independent scores (Step 17)   full curve
##   5. Basic FSSM (Step 10, diag H/diag Q)    full curve, level source SHARED
##                                             with #6 (see design note above)
##   6. Final FSSM (Step 11 preferred H/Q + Step 12/13 preferred level)  full curve
##
## NO RE-ESTIMATION AT ANY ORIGIN (Requirement 3, explicitly justified): every
## model's parameters were already estimated ONCE on the original training
## window (Steps 10-17). Only the FORECAST ORIGIN advances; frozen parameters
## are applied recursively from each origin using ONLY information through
## that origin (Requirement: "no future information leaking into training").
## =============================================================================


