## =============================================================================
## STEP 19 — STATISTICAL COMPARISON AND ROBUSTNESS ASSESSMENT OF GROUNDWATER
##           FORECASTING MODELS
## Project : Hourly Groundwater Level (GWL) analysis — well GT2648C03
## Continues directly from STEP 18 (data_clean/18_rolling_origin_validation.rds)
## and reuses Steps 7, 9, 11, 12/13's own already-computed specification-
## comparison tables for the sensitivity analysis (Requirement 6).
## =============================================================================
## SCOPE NOTE (stated explicitly, not hidden): Requirement 6 asks for
## sensitivity across FIVE factors (K, m, H/Q structure, seasonal spec,
## training window). A full nested rolling-origin re-validation (Step 18,
## repeated per combination) is computationally prohibitive to run honestly
## inside this deliverable. FOUR factors (K, m, H/Q, seasonal spec) are
## therefore assessed using the GENUINE, already-computed candidate-grid
## comparison tables Steps 7/9/11/12-13 produced themselves -- reused, not
## re-derived. The FIFTH factor (training-window choice) has no existing
## alternative-window result anywhere in this project, so ONE new, narrowly-
## scoped perturbation is performed here (h=1 only, level model only) and
## explicitly labelled as new computation.
## =============================================================================


## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
## 1. PACKAGES
## -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
required_packages <- c("dplyr", "tidyr", "lubridate", "ggplot2", "writexl",
                       "scales", "purrr", "KFAS")
