    "  [FORMAL TEST] Mann-Kendall tau = ", mk_tau, " (p = ", mk_p, "), Sen's slope = ", sens_slope,
    " GWL units/year (monthly means, Step 4). This is the formally-tested,\n",
    "  autocorrelation-robust trend estimate -- see Step 4 for the full descriptive-\n",
    "  vs-formal distinction maintained throughout this project.\n\n", sep = "")

cat("SEASONALITY:\n",
    "  Annual seasonality was ", ifelse(seasonality_supported, "SUPPORTED", "NOT clearly supported"),
    " for the daily-level model by Step 13's formal BIC + out-of-sample forecast\n",
    "  evidence (harmonic-regression ladder, K=0..4). Any seasonal pattern found is a\n",
    "  STATISTICAL, calendar-time regularity -- NOT evidence of a specific recharge,\n",
    "  discharge, or pumping mechanism (Step 13's explicit caution, repeated here).\n\n", sep = "")

cat("FUNCTIONAL VARIABILITY:\n",
    "  Step 6's exact orthogonal decomposition: ", between_pct, "% of total day-hour GWL\n",
    "  variation is between-day LEVEL change; ", within_pct, "% is within-day SHAPE variation.\n",
    "  This is why the project modelled level (Steps 12-13) and shape (Steps 7-11)\n",
    "  SEPARATELY rather than letting FPCA rediscover the trend already characterized\n",
    "  in Step 4.\n\n", sep = "")

cat("MEANING OF MAJOR FPCs (CAUTION, NOT CAUSAL):\n",
    "  The leading FPCA eigenfunctions (Fig07) are, mathematically, ONLY directions of\n",
    "  maximal variance in the CENTERED within-day shape curves -- orthogonal patterns\n",
    "  a domain expert might cautiously describe by shape (e.g. 'rises through the\n",
    "  afternoon') but which carry NO built-in hydrological label. Any physical reading\n",
    "  (recharge, pumping, barometric, tidal) requires independent hydrogeological\n",
    "  evidence about well GT2648C03, not just curve shape (Step 8's explicit caution,\n",
    "  upheld here).\n\n", sep = "")

cat("DOES DYNAMIC STATE EVOLUTION (Q>0) IMPROVE PREDICTION?\n",
    "  Preferred structure (Step 11): ", step11_results$preferred_structure$structure, ".\n",
    "  Likelihood-ratio tests (Q=0 vs Q>0) are, as expected with n_train~1748, almost\n",
    "  always statistically significant -- NOT strong evidence on their own (Step 11's\n",
    "  explicit caution about over-powered LR tests at this sample size). The more\n",
    "  informative comparison is OUT-OF-SAMPLE forecast RMSE, Q=0 vs Q>0 variants,\n",
    "  reported in Step 11's q_evidence_table and reproduced in Table 4 above.\n\n", sep = "")

cat("DOES THE PROPOSED GWL-FSSM BEAT PERSISTENCE?\n",
    "  At h=1: Final FSSM RMSE = ", round(h1_row$RMSE, 5), " vs. Persistence RMSE = ", round(persist_row$RMSE, 5),
    " (", improvement_h1$pct_RMSE_improvement, "% RMSE improvement).\n",
    "  Recall (Step 15): lag-1 hourly autocorrelation = ", round(lag1_acf, 5),
    " -- persistence is a genuinely strong, not token, comparator for this series.\n\n", sep = "")

cat("AT WHAT HORIZONS DOES IT PROVIDE USEFUL IMPROVEMENT?\n",
