## =============================================================================
## FINAL MASTER-RESULTS ARCHIVE — GWL-FSSM WORKFLOW, STEPS 1-26
## Project : Hourly Groundwater Level (GWL) analysis — well GT2648C03
## =============================================================================
## PURPOSE
## Collect the already-existing objects produced by Steps 1-26 (run earlier in
## this same R session) into ONE structured, documented list and save it as a
## single .rds file, so the complete analysis can later be reloaded with:
##   GWL_master_results <- readRDS("data_clean/GWL_FSSM_Steps01_26_MasterResults.rds")
##
## This block does NOT rerun, refit, or recompute anything. It only reads
## objects that already exist in the current R session (created by Steps
## 1-26), checks for their presence with exists()/get0(), organizes them into
## a nested list, builds an object inventory, verifies the saved file, and
## reports any expected object that could not be found -- it never invents or
## fabricates a missing object.
##
## Real object names used below (verified against the actual Steps 1-26 code,
## not guessed):
##   Step 1  : gwl_raw, gwl_summary_stats, dupe_timestamps, plausible_min,
##             plausible_max, expected_datetime_col, expected_gwl_col
##   Step 2  : timestamp_QC_results
##   Step 3  : gwl_regularized, gap_events, method_selection_by_gap_length,
##             duplicate_resolution_log, offset_alignment_log,
##             imputation_summary, before_after_comparison
